\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces DASF-Net. (a) The dual-branch encoder: one utterance becomes a sparse cepstral and a dense spectral view, each passed through its own adapter stem into a single weight-shared Xception trunk. (b) CASF tokenises both feature maps, lets each view attend over the other, and combines them through a learned gate into $z$; three heads then act on $z$, the language head behind a gradient reversal layer.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dasfnet}{{2}{5}{DASF-Net. (a) The dual-branch encoder: one utterance becomes a sparse cepstral and a dense spectral view, each passed through its own adapter stem into a single weight-shared Xception trunk. (b) CASF tokenises both feature maps, lets each view attend over the other, and combines them through a learned gate into $z$; three heads then act on $z$, the language head behind a gradient reversal layer}{figure.2}{}}
